1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:08,000
Marco runs a one-person moving company in Lugano.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:16,500
Leads arrive at 21:00, in Italian and in German.

3
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:24,800
He quotes by hand. Whoever answers first gets the job.

4
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:31,500
Quotelet Aperto: he writes his prices in plain German.

5
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:39,000
Apertus turns the text into a calculator config.

6
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:47,000
The validator checks it: 4 fields, formula OK.

7
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:56,000
Prices stay a checked formula in code. Apertus never does the math.

8
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:04,800
Live preview in de-CH with CHF. Copy the link or the embed code.

9
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:13,000
The customer opens the link. The config lives in the URL, nothing is stored.

10
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:24,000
20 m³, 3rd floor, no lift.

11
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:34,800
A range with VAT, computed and formatted by Quotelet core.

12
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:42,000
Message language: Italian. Apertus writes the words only.

13
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:49,000
French, German: the amounts come from core, never from the model.

14
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:54,800
WhatsApp gets the Italian text with the same amounts.

15
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:01,000
Now a vague price list: "a bit more on Sundays".

16
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:08,000
The validator rejects it. One repair try asks for a number.

17
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:14,800
Still no number, so the errors are shown. No guessed prices.

18
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:23,000
Public eval: 30 price lists, 4 languages, 8B vs 70B.

19
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:31,000
Valid configs, quote match, latency and cost per calculator.

20
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:39,800
These rows are a dry run of the harness. Real Apertus numbers come next.

21
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:47,500
Open weights: self-host Apertus with vLLM or Ollama, same env vars.

22
00:02:47,500 --> 00:02:54,800
No database, no cookies. Price lists and quotes stay with you.

23
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:58,300
Quotelet Aperto. Plain words in, checked calculators out.
